{"shortDescription":"The Australian dollar weakened to around $0.70, hitting a seven-week low as markets weighed mixed labor-market figures for clues on the policy outlook.The jobless rate rose to 4.6%, above forecasts of a steady 4.5% and the highest since late 2021, while the economy added 39,500 jobs versus a predic…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Australian dollar weakened to around $0.70, hitting a seven-week low as markets weighed mixed labor-market figures for clues on the policy outlook."]},{"type":"p","children":["The jobless rate rose to 4.6%, above forecasts of a steady 4.5% and the highest since late 2021, while the economy added 39,500 jobs versus a predicted 20,000 increase."]},{"type":"p","children":["The report was the final major economic release before the Reserve Bank's September 28–29 meeting and showed signs of softening in a labor market the central bank has described as still “a bit tight,” potentially easing domestic inflation pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets still price an 86% chance of a 25-bp hike to 4.60% in September, but down from 95% before the jobs report, while the odds of another move fall to 44% for November."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, a firmer US dollar added pressure on the Aussie as stronger-than-expected economic data reinforced bets on further Fed rate hikes."]},{"type":"p","children":["Rising oil prices also weighed on global risk appetite after Iran cast doubt on progress in peace talks."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:586312:0","title":"Australian Dollar Hits 7-Week Low","published":1790216345,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/australia/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:AUDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/AU","logo":{"sty